==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|stinga|lang=non}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{recons|stinganan|lang=gem-pro}}. Compare Faroese and Swedish {{term|stinga|lang=fo}}, English {{term|sting|lang=en}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈstiŋka/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|iŋka|lang=is}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-strong|stakk|stungu|stungið}}

# {{ambitransitive|governs the accusative}} to [[stab]], to [[sting]], to [[prick]]
# {{ambitransitive|governs the accusative}} to [[wound]], to [[hurt]]{{jump|is|hurt|s}}
# {{transitive|governs the dative}} to [[prick]] with something, to [[stab]] with something
#: ''Hann '''stakk''' hnífnum í borðið.''
#:: He '''sticked''' the knife in the table.
# {{transitive|governs the dative}} to [[slip]] something, to [[put]] something
#: ''Prinsessan '''stakk''' einhverju í vasa bóndans.''
#:: The princess '''slipped''' something into the farmer's pocket.
#: ''Hún hætti lestri og '''stakk''' skruddunni í hilluna.''
#:: She stopped reading and '''put''' the old book into the shelf.
# {{context|impersonal|lang=is}} to [[strike]] someone
#: ''Það '''stakk''' mig.''
#:: It '''struck''' me.

